{
  "description": "issue #675 (SP3): `ask` restores the previous `tell` set, not just the default. `tell :a` sets the persistent set to turtle 1; `ask :b [ … ]` addresses turtle 2 only for the block; the trailing `forward 30` returns to turtle 1 — the set restored after the scoped `ask`. Every change of the addressed set — here from `ask`/`tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }`, so a consumer can identify the addressed turtle set (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193); `ask`/`each` emit one again when the previous set is restored, on every exit path.",
